    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "80294ffa_153751ea",
        "filename": "java/sdk_library.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1003,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-19T14:22:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is no need for it to be a drop in replacement. The java_sdk_library_import is intended to provide the API for the module, it is not intended to build the module itself. That would be like trying to build Android using the SDK we provide developers.\n\nHaving the prebuilt and source coexisting in one build is I think an achievable goal (and something you and I put a lot of work into with jsl/jsli) but we cannot build a module against its own prebuilts.",
      "parentUuid": "37884530_8cbefb21",
      "revId": "56d4490d59568476ad9eafdc385ab9bd1ac242f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7b269fd1_29ac94b1",
        "filename": "java/sdk_library.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1003,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-19T14:25:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ok then do you think we need to break when java_sdk_library_import is depended on by a module that doesn\u0027t have sdk_version? I think so.",
      "parentUuid": "80294ffa_153751ea",
      "revId": "56d4490d59568476ad9eafdc385ab9bd1ac242f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5aa12cc_87338a67",
        "filename": "java/sdk_library.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1003,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-19T14:32:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No I don\u0027t. Just because module \"X\" depends on \"foo.impl\" when built against java_sdk_library does not mean that it requires access to the implementation. It is just getting the implementation because there is at least one module that does not specify sdk_version and which requires the implementation of one of the java_sdk_library instances on which it depends.\n\nIf you caused the build to break (rather than relied on compilation to check whether the implementation was actually needed) then you would potentially break working builds.\n\nBy allowing developers to be explicit about what they need we can avoid this issue of lowest common denominator.\n\nI had added another comment to the bug you raised to cover this specific case.",
      "parentUuid": "7b269fd1_29ac94b1",
      "revId": "56d4490d59568476ad9eafdc385ab9bd1ac242f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    }
